00:30:34,340 --> 00:30:46,020
And this is an important message for our day and age because there is a temptation to fixate on that first part of the message that Jesus is a salvation prepared for all people.

446
00:30:46,020 --> 00:30:58,420
And there's this kind of universalist idea that's seeping its way into Christianity that everyone is blessed by God and that everyone will be saved no matter what they do, no matter what they think, no matter how they act, no matter what happens.

447
00:30:58,560 --> 00:31:06,540
Jesus is salvation for all, yes, he's salvation that's available for all, but it has to be received.

448
00:31:06,540 --> 00:31:12,420
It has to be a gift that people are willing to come under the lordship and leadership of Jesus in their life.

449
00:31:12,420 --> 00:31:18,420
Yes, Jesus is a gift that is available for all, but he will be rejected by many.

450
00:31:18,420 --> 00:31:32,600
I think about 1 Corinthians 1 where Paul says the message of the cross is foolish to those who are headed for destruction, but to us who are being saved, we know that it is the very power of God.

451
00:31:32,600 --> 00:31:42,380
Like the crucifixion, the death, burial, and resurrection of Jesus is a very important point in history where oftentimes people divide.

452
00:31:43,180 --> 00:31:48,160
A lot of people want to say, yeah, he's a good teacher, a wise teacher, he has helpful ideologies.

453
00:31:48,160 --> 00:31:51,280
It's nice that we love our neighbor as ourself.

454
00:31:51,280 --> 00:31:56,540
But this whole resurrection from the dead thing is not for me.

455
00:31:56,540 --> 00:32:04,600
Salvation is available to all, but often, a lot of times, people will trip over.

456
00:32:04,600 --> 00:32:22,240
And again, going back to the specific culture, ideology message, I think the church that I grew up in tended to say the type of people that would trip over the message of Jesus are sinners.

457
00:32:22,240 --> 00:32:24,040
Those sinners.

458
00:32:25,240 --> 00:32:35,920
And the reality is, when we look at the life of Jesus, the poor, the powerless, the broken, the hurting, those are the people that actually received the message of Jesus.

459
00:32:35,920 --> 00:32:44,840
It was the religious people, the good Christians, the good Jewish people, the good people in the temple that often tripped over the message of Jesus.

460
00:32:44,840 --> 00:32:53,240
So I just want to think about a couple of types of people that rejected the message of Jesus throughout his days.

461
00:32:53,240 --> 00:32:55,340
We've got the Pharisees, right?

462
00:32:55,340 --> 00:33:00,500
So often, the Pharisees have the most problem with Jesus' message.

463
00:33:00,500 --> 00:33:00,800
Why?

464
00:33:00,800 --> 00:33:03,660
Because they had power and control.

465
00:33:03,660 --> 00:33:09,020
And Jesus was asking them to lay down their power and control to serve other people.

466
00:33:09,020 --> 00:33:10,180
And they didn't want to do that.

467
00:33:10,180 --> 00:33:14,760
They got too comfortable with the power and control that they had built over time.

468
00:33:14,760 --> 00:33:17,080
And so they tripped over the message of Jesus.

469
00:33:17,080 --> 00:33:19,580
They rejected the message of Jesus.

470
00:33:19,580 --> 00:33:21,220
Why?

471
00:33:21,220 --> 00:33:25,160
Because they didn't want to give up their power, their influence, their control.

472
00:33:25,160 --> 00:33:28,480
They didn't want to actually lay down their lives to serve other people.

473
00:33:28,480 --> 00:33:34,140
This is the type of people that trip over the message of Jesus, that ultimately reject the message of Jesus.

474
00:33:35,240 --> 00:33:40,680
Another reason you might wrestle with or reject the message of Jesus is intellectual.

475
00:33:40,680 --> 00:33:45,340
There's another group that hung out with the Pharisees called the Sadducees.

476
00:33:45,340 --> 00:33:48,740
And the Sadducees were very intellectual people.

477
00:33:48,740 --> 00:33:51,880
They were very secularly, culturally driven people.

478
00:33:51,880 --> 00:33:55,500
They didn't believe in any supernatural stuff, right?

479
00:33:55,500 --> 00:33:58,260
They didn't believe that resurrection from the dead was possible.

480
00:33:58,260 --> 00:34:01,660
And so their problem with Jesus' message was intellectual.

481
00:34:02,380 --> 00:34:07,920
Like, hey, you're teaching whatever, like this is weird, but like resurrection from the dead, that doesn't happen.

482
00:34:07,920 --> 00:34:10,120
When you die, you die, it's over.

483
00:34:10,120 --> 00:34:13,480
And their problem with Jesus was intellectual.

484
00:34:13,480 --> 00:34:16,220
I think this is an issue of our culture today.

485
00:34:16,220 --> 00:34:21,260
Like a lot of people miss the message of Jesus because they have intellectual hang-ups.

486
00:34:21,260 --> 00:34:27,040
And I want to be honest and hear those intellectual hang-ups and dialogue with you about those conversations.

487
00:34:27,040 --> 00:34:32,860
But if you're here and you're still kind of rejecting the message of Jesus because you have intellectual hang-ups,

488
00:34:32,860 --> 00:34:47,060
man, I'd invite you to lean into that conversation because I don't think that that's a hang-up that should keep you from coming under the lordship and leadership of Jesus.

489
00:34:47,060 --> 00:34:48,140
So maybe it's religion.

490
00:34:48,440 --> 00:34:53,040
Maybe you want to be in control of your own situation, intellectual issues that you might have.

491
00:34:53,040 --> 00:35:02,700
Or maybe you just really like the life that you have right now and you don't want anybody to tell you what to do with your money or your time or your energy or your relationships.

492
00:35:02,700 --> 00:35:04,640
Maybe you just want to be in charge of your own life.

493
00:35:04,640 --> 00:35:12,400
Or think about the rich young ruler who came to Jesus and said, what must I do to enter your eternal life?

494
00:35:12,400 --> 00:35:15,980
Jesus said, sell everything and give it to the poor.

495
00:35:15,980 --> 00:35:17,640
Come, follow me.

496
00:35:17,640 --> 00:35:20,520
So the rich young ruler walked away sad.

497
00:35:20,520 --> 00:35:26,760
Some people tricked over the message of Jesus because they're so invested in this temporary life.

498
00:35:26,760 --> 00:35:33,180
They're so invested in what they have right here, right now, and building their own kingdom and building their own empire.

499
00:35:33,480 --> 00:35:36,340
Then Jesus says, I need to be in charge of those things.

500
00:35:36,340 --> 00:35:39,920
I need to be the Lord and leader of your life.

501
00:35:39,920 --> 00:35:46,040
And we don't like that because we like to be the Lord and leader of our own life until we run everything into the ground.

502
00:35:46,040 --> 00:35:48,360
And then we're like, God, where were you?

503
00:35:48,360 --> 00:35:49,260
What happened?

504
00:35:49,260 --> 00:35:50,760
And he's like, you did this.

505
00:35:50,760 --> 00:35:52,260
Like, what do you want from me?

506
00:35:52,260 --> 00:35:53,920
I've been asking you for control.

507
00:35:53,920 --> 00:35:56,080
You know, let's go back to Carrie Underwood.

508
00:35:56,080 --> 00:35:58,800
Like, I've been asking you to give me the wheel for a while now.

509
00:35:58,800 --> 00:36:02,080
I saw you were headed towards the cliff and you didn't want to do anything with it.

510
00:36:02,080 --> 00:36:07,580
But we have a gracious God who, even after we run into the cliff, if we're willing to say, hey, God, I did that.

511
00:36:07,580 --> 00:36:08,920
That was me.

512
00:36:08,920 --> 00:36:10,140
Can you help me?

513
00:36:10,140 --> 00:36:15,040
I have a God that is willing to take over in those situations.

514
00:36:15,220 --> 00:36:19,380
And then we just have a culture in America where we're just so self-sufficient.

515
00:36:19,380 --> 00:36:22,960
We just have everything we could ever want, need, or imagine.

516
00:36:22,960 --> 00:36:31,600
And Jesus, he addressed this in his teaching when he said, it's going to be really hard for rich people to inherit the kingdom of God.

517
00:36:31,600 --> 00:36:34,740
It's going to be like a camel trying to get through the eye of a needle.

518
00:36:36,060 --> 00:36:39,740
And I think that term, rich people, we tend to disassociate with that.

519
00:36:39,740 --> 00:36:42,820
But if you're here in this room today, you would be considered rich.

520
00:36:42,820 --> 00:36:44,880
We're self-sufficient.

521
00:36:44,880 --> 00:36:47,340
We have everything that we could ever need.

522
00:36:47,340 --> 00:36:50,940
Or imagine, I had a friend that was a youth pastor in Cary, North Carolina.

523
00:36:50,940 --> 00:36:53,680
And Cary is a booming area in the tech industry.

524
00:36:53,680 --> 00:36:56,280
And just everybody's wealthy in Cary.

525
00:36:56,280 --> 00:37:05,080
And he said, he told me, he said, it's so hard to teach teenagers that they need Jesus when they've never needed anything in their entire life.

526
00:37:05,080 --> 00:37:09,340
And that's true with most of us.

527
00:37:09,340 --> 00:37:15,820
Like, it's so hard for us to actually acknowledge that we need the leadership of Jesus in our life.

528
00:37:15,820 --> 00:37:21,500
And we've pretty much been able to get through life on our own, with our own power and our own strength.

529
00:37:22,400 --> 00:37:28,440
See, the message of Simeon is Jesus is a gift of salvation that's available to all.

530
00:37:28,440 --> 00:37:34,520
But it's going to be rejected by many because many people want to hold on to their life.

531
00:37:34,520 --> 00:37:42,320
Jesus would be born and grow up, and he would teach his disciples this in Matthew chapter 16.

532
00:37:42,320 --> 00:37:50,520
Jesus said to his disciples, if any of you wants to be my follower, you must give up your own way.

533
00:37:51,580 --> 00:37:53,900
Take up your cross and follow me.

534
00:37:53,900 --> 00:37:57,060
If you try to hang on to your life, you will lose it.

535
00:37:57,060 --> 00:38:02,160
But if you give up your life for my sake, you will find it.

536
00:38:02,160 --> 00:38:05,520
This is the message of Jesus.

537
00:38:05,520 --> 00:38:07,400
This is the gift of salvation.

538
00:38:07,400 --> 00:38:09,020
Give up your life.

539
00:38:09,020 --> 00:38:14,400
Lay down your life at the foot of the cross and follow Jesus.

540
00:38:14,620 --> 00:38:19,040
Be willing to die, to give up your own way, to take up your cross and follow me.

541
00:38:19,040 --> 00:38:22,580
And this is why people reject Jesus.

542
00:38:22,580 --> 00:38:25,760
Because we're prideful.

543
00:38:25,760 --> 00:38:26,420
We're selfish.

544
00:38:26,420 --> 00:38:32,020
We have the same thing going on that Adam and Eve had going on, which is they just wanted to be in charge.

545
00:38:32,020 --> 00:38:33,980
We want to be in charge.

546
00:38:33,980 --> 00:38:35,880
It feels nice.

547
00:38:36,700 --> 00:38:40,220
But at the end of the day, it leads to destruction.

548
00:38:40,220 --> 00:38:54,260
To keep it Christmas-themed, the best way I can illustrate it is to kind of keep in and steal from C.S. Lewis.

549
00:38:55,100 --> 00:39:01,320
And as I think about this, like, salvation is a gift that's available for all but will be rejected by many.

550
00:39:01,320 --> 00:39:04,980
I think about a child with two Christmas gifts under the tree.

551
00:39:04,980 --> 00:39:09,320
They open up the first gift in excitement, and it's a remote-control car.

552
00:39:09,320 --> 00:39:12,740
And they're just pumped about the remote-control car.

553
00:39:12,740 --> 00:39:14,100
They're wheeling it around everywhere.

554
00:39:14,100 --> 00:39:15,520
They're slamming it into things.

555
00:39:15,520 --> 00:39:17,060
It's exciting.

556
00:39:17,060 --> 00:39:17,820
It's awesome.

557
00:39:17,820 --> 00:39:21,760
And their parents are like, there's another gift.

558
00:39:21,760 --> 00:39:23,280
Like, don't forget your other gift.

559
00:39:23,340 --> 00:39:26,380
And they're just so infatuated, excited with the original gift.

560
00:39:26,380 --> 00:39:31,380
And what's wrapped under the tree, the second gift, is batteries.

561
00:39:31,380 --> 00:39:36,900
Like, the source, the very source of the gift that they were given.

562
00:39:36,900 --> 00:39:44,440
But they're so tripped up on the fun aspect of the car.

563
00:39:44,440 --> 00:39:47,880
They're just playing with this toy, and they're using it.

564
00:39:47,880 --> 00:39:50,840
But they're not using it in the way that it was created to be used.

565
00:39:51,980 --> 00:39:54,800
And God's saying, hey, there's more to this gift.

566
00:39:54,800 --> 00:39:55,960
It's available to you.

567
00:39:55,960 --> 00:39:57,240
All you have to do is open it.

568
00:39:57,240 --> 00:40:05,340
All you have to do is receive it, and you'll realize that the very source of life for the gift that you've been given is right here, available to all.

569
00:40:05,340 --> 00:40:06,640
But you have to receive it.

570
00:40:06,640 --> 00:40:07,660
You have to open it up.

571
00:40:07,660 --> 00:40:10,200
You have to put it in the vehicle.

572
00:40:11,360 --> 00:40:23,800
See, oftentimes, we treat our lives like that first gift, and we just go after it, use it in ways that it was not created to be used.

573
00:40:23,800 --> 00:40:25,600
And it's fun for a season.

574
00:40:27,600 --> 00:40:29,300
It's not what we were created to do.

575
00:40:29,300 --> 00:40:34,040
The Bible says in Ecclesiastes 3, verse 11, that God has put eternity in each of our hearts.

576
00:40:34,040 --> 00:40:38,820
Like, there's a spot for a battery inside of our souls.

577
00:40:38,820 --> 00:40:49,060
There's a God spot in our souls that we need to fuel this life, to give us eternal aspect, to give us this abundant life that Jesus promised.

578
00:40:49,180 --> 00:40:56,100
But so often, we're so content with just playing with the temporary gifts that God's given us while missing the eternal gift.

579
00:40:56,100 --> 00:40:59,700
Instead, I stole from C.S. Lewis.

580
00:40:59,700 --> 00:41:02,420
He says it much more eloquently when he says,

581
00:41:02,420 --> 00:41:10,080
We are half-hearted creatures, fooling about with drink and sex and ambition when infinite joy is offered to us,

582
00:41:10,080 --> 00:41:14,220
like an ignorant child who wants to keep on making mud pies in a slum

583
00:41:14,220 --> 00:41:19,280
because he cannot imagine what is meant by the offering of a holiday at the sea.

584
00:41:19,280 --> 00:41:21,920
We are far too easily pleased.

585
00:41:21,920 --> 00:41:27,140
The gift of salvation is available to all, but it will be rejected by many,

586
00:41:27,140 --> 00:41:30,900
mostly because we're far too easily pleased with this temporary life,

587
00:41:30,900 --> 00:41:35,980
that we can't even imagine the gift of eternity that God has offered to us.

588
00:41:35,980 --> 00:41:43,580
And I hope that we're a people that are willing to lay down the temporary aspects of this life

589
00:41:43,580 --> 00:41:45,100
in order to follow Jesus.

590
00:41:45,100 --> 00:41:49,200
Bring this full circle.

591
00:41:49,200 --> 00:41:55,280
What does Simeon say when he holds the Savior Jesus?

592
00:41:55,280 --> 00:42:02,220
Sovereign Lord, now let your servant die in peace.

593
00:42:02,220 --> 00:42:08,400
Simeon realized that Jesus was worth losing his life for.

594
00:42:11,020 --> 00:42:16,540
That it was worth it to just go ahead and die and enter paradise

595
00:42:16,540 --> 00:42:20,940
because he'd seen the Savior of the world, the Messiah, Jesus.

596
00:42:20,940 --> 00:42:24,540
Jesus is a gift available for all, but he will be rejected by many.

597
00:42:24,540 --> 00:42:26,420
What is our response?

598
00:42:26,420 --> 00:42:32,260
Will we be willing to lay down our life, our temporary life,

599
00:42:32,260 --> 00:42:35,380
to receive the eternal gift of salvation?

600
00:42:35,580 --> 00:42:43,640
Or will we hold tightly to our stuff, our money, our resources, our time, our talents, our families, our relationships?

601
00:42:43,640 --> 00:42:45,380
Are we just going to hold tightly?

602
00:42:49,560 --> 00:42:51,620
So, I encourage you.

603
00:42:51,620 --> 00:42:52,340
Take Simeon home.

604
00:42:52,340 --> 00:42:56,760
Put him in your nativity scene or somewhere that he can see.

605
00:42:56,760 --> 00:43:02,280
And whenever you think about it, think about his message to Mary and Joseph.

606
00:43:02,280 --> 00:43:06,580
Jesus is a gift of salvation available to all of us.

607
00:43:06,580 --> 00:43:08,920
He's going to be rejected by many.

608
00:43:09,180 --> 00:43:11,620
And if you're in here and you're not sure where you're at with Jesus,

609
00:43:11,620 --> 00:43:17,040
I pray that when you look at him, you think, like, have I received this gift?

610
00:43:17,040 --> 00:43:18,620
Or am I still rejected?

611
00:43:18,620 --> 00:43:24,000
Am I willing to lay down my life to lose it all in order to follow Jesus?

612
00:43:24,000 --> 00:43:27,700
And if you're here and you're a follower of Jesus,

613
00:43:27,700 --> 00:43:31,620
I pray that when you look at Simeon and you think about people in your life,

614
00:43:32,420 --> 00:43:38,820
that you can extend that gift, that you can intentionally share the message of Jesus with.

615
00:43:38,820 --> 00:43:45,960
Because I think oftentimes once we receive it, we tend to move on and forget about everybody else.

616
00:43:45,960 --> 00:43:54,180
So, let's be a people who realize that Jesus is a gift of salvation available to all.

617
00:43:54,180 --> 00:44:00,860
Let's be a people who live in light of the fact that God always delivers on his promises.

618
00:44:00,860 --> 00:44:02,140
Let's pray.

619
00:44:02,780 --> 00:44:03,660
Father, we love you.

620
00:44:03,660 --> 00:44:05,360
We thank you for Simeon.

621
00:44:05,360 --> 00:44:08,900
We thank you for this message that you shared through him.

622
00:44:08,900 --> 00:44:18,480
Pray that we would be a people that would realize that your salvation is free.

623
00:44:18,480 --> 00:44:19,560
It's available.

624
00:44:19,560 --> 00:44:21,480
It has to be open.

625
00:44:21,480 --> 00:44:22,640
It has to be received.

626
00:44:22,640 --> 00:44:27,160
Pray that we'd live in light of that truth this Christmas season.

627
00:44:27,160 --> 00:44:28,900
That we'd share that truth with others.

628
00:44:28,900 --> 00:44:34,080
That we'd be unashamed and unapologetic about the free message of salvation through Jesus.

629
00:44:34,080 --> 00:44:36,200
In Jesus' name I pray.

630
00:44:36,200 --> 00:44:37,280
Amen.

631
00:44:41,840 --> 00:44:43,300
We're going to...

632
00:44:43,300 --> 00:44:44,860
Hi guys.

633
00:44:44,860 --> 00:44:45,380
My name's Andy.

634
00:44:45,380 --> 00:44:46,080
Hi.

635
00:44:46,080 --> 00:44:47,080
Thanks.

636
00:44:47,080 --> 00:44:48,760
I don't do this much anymore.

637
00:44:48,760 --> 00:44:50,880
You're welcome.

638
00:44:50,880 --> 00:44:54,320
We're going to take communion.

639
00:44:55,080 --> 00:44:57,340
And then I'm going to talk a little bit more than you want me to.

640
00:44:57,340 --> 00:44:59,420
And then we're going to leave.

641
00:44:59,420 --> 00:45:02,800
But please don't leave this place like you leave a theater.

642
00:45:02,800 --> 00:45:05,980
Leave this place like you leave a church.

643
00:45:07,720 --> 00:45:11,180
We in the Alamo, we have a bigger lobby than we will ever have.

644
00:45:11,180 --> 00:45:12,660
Ever.

645
00:45:12,660 --> 00:45:17,440
If God gives us a giant pole barn in the country or somewhere in the city, which we prefer.

646
00:45:17,440 --> 00:45:20,140
We're never going to have a lobby like this.

647
00:45:20,140 --> 00:45:22,580
So, find someone when you leave.

648
00:45:22,580 --> 00:45:26,060
And they're just like, hey, your kids are as tall as my kids.

649
00:45:26,060 --> 00:45:27,580
Let's go see Christmas lights later.

650
00:45:27,580 --> 00:45:33,500
Like, hey, you like the same athletic competitions that I also enjoy viewing.

651
00:45:34,080 --> 00:45:35,120
Let's do that together.

652
00:45:35,120 --> 00:45:37,000
Hey, here's a giant lobby.

653
00:45:37,000 --> 00:45:37,860
Let's get french fries.

654
00:45:37,860 --> 00:45:41,700
Like, do those things.

655
00:45:41,700 --> 00:45:44,560
Now it's going to feel forced and we're all like, too cool for that.

656
00:45:44,560 --> 00:45:47,380
But, leave like you leave a church.

657
00:45:47,380 --> 00:45:51,120
Leave like you leave a place full of people who enjoy and love the same God.

658
00:45:51,120 --> 00:45:53,840
And want to invest in each other and learn from each other.

659
00:45:53,840 --> 00:45:56,040
And want our families to grow up together.

660
00:45:56,040 --> 00:45:58,420
And give a heck.

661
00:45:58,420 --> 00:46:01,720
So, sorry, soapbox.

662
00:46:03,620 --> 00:46:04,720
We're going to celebrate communion.

663
00:46:04,720 --> 00:46:08,640
So, if you have your little communion lunchable, whip those out.

664
00:46:08,640 --> 00:46:11,260
There are more on your way in.

665
00:46:11,260 --> 00:46:14,420
We use these to teach us humility.

666
00:46:14,420 --> 00:46:23,740
As we recognize that all of creation and consumable packaging cries out longing to be redeemed.

667
00:46:23,740 --> 00:46:29,020
So, you can start opening those because it's a ginger process.

668
00:46:29,020 --> 00:46:32,740
In a room this size, 15 of us are going to spill them.

669
00:46:33,000 --> 00:46:33,500
And that's okay.

670
00:46:33,500 --> 00:46:38,920
It's Advent season.

671
00:46:38,920 --> 00:46:41,520
And some of you grew up with really strong Advent traditions.

672
00:46:41,520 --> 00:46:42,880
And some of you did not.

673
00:46:42,880 --> 00:46:43,740
And that's okay.

674
00:46:43,740 --> 00:46:46,840
We don't have a strong Advent tradition at campus.

675
00:46:46,840 --> 00:46:48,600
We're a mongrel people.

676
00:46:48,600 --> 00:46:51,080
And so, we kind of build as we go.

677
00:46:51,080 --> 00:46:56,280
But Advent is, like Ryan said earlier, it's a season of anticipation.

678
00:46:56,280 --> 00:46:59,620
We look back and we celebrate the anticipation.

679
00:46:59,620 --> 00:47:09,060
We celebrate and we look back gratefully for those long periods of silence when God's people were waiting for a Messiah to be born.

680
00:47:09,700 --> 00:47:11,760
And we can relate to that because we're also waiting.

681
00:47:11,760 --> 00:47:27,400
So, as we think of all those verses from Handel's Messiah, all those verses in Isaiah and Habakkuk and Malachi, where God promised his people that the king was coming.

682
00:47:28,240 --> 00:47:31,200
And then people like Simeon, who got to see the promise.

683
00:47:31,200 --> 00:47:32,500
And Simeon was rare.

684
00:47:33,500 --> 00:47:35,820
Most of God's people didn't see that promise.

685
00:47:35,820 --> 00:47:37,880
That Simeon was chosen and blessed.

686
00:47:37,880 --> 00:47:40,460
And that's an honor that maybe we'll see.

687
00:47:40,460 --> 00:47:40,960
We don't know.

688
00:47:40,960 --> 00:47:44,260
At Christmas, we celebrate the birth of that king.

689
00:47:44,260 --> 00:47:47,600
Every week, we celebrate his life with communion.

690
00:47:47,600 --> 00:47:54,120
This is something, if you're not new to, or if you are new to church or you're new to Christianity, this is a weird thing that we do.

691
00:47:54,120 --> 00:47:55,640
It might be the weirdest thing we do here.

692
00:47:55,640 --> 00:48:00,280
Because we don't run cows excitingly or play with reptiles or anything.

693
00:48:00,500 --> 00:48:03,940
But we're going to eat the little Starzomi cracker.

694
00:48:03,940 --> 00:48:05,820
And we're going to drink the really terrible juice.

695
00:48:05,820 --> 00:48:07,200
And we're going to think about Jesus.

696
00:48:07,200 --> 00:48:10,240
And we're going to do that because he asked us to do it.

697
00:48:10,240 --> 00:48:13,080
As a way, when we get together, to remember him.

698
00:48:13,080 --> 00:48:15,820
And remember that he wasn't just a baby.

699
00:48:15,820 --> 00:48:21,180
If all of Christmas is about Jesus being born as a baby, Christmas is cool.

700
00:48:21,180 --> 00:48:23,520
But we're all born.

701
00:48:23,520 --> 00:48:27,580
It's because of who the baby was and what he meant and what he is.

702
00:48:27,580 --> 00:48:29,120
And who we are because of that.

703
00:48:29,920 --> 00:48:32,340
So, go ahead and get out your cracker.

704
00:48:32,340 --> 00:48:36,040
We're going to take this.

705
00:48:36,040 --> 00:48:38,000
And as we do it, we're going to think about the life of Jesus.

706
00:48:38,000 --> 00:48:39,820
How he healed people.

707
00:48:39,820 --> 00:48:40,840
Who he loved.

708
00:48:40,840 --> 00:48:42,980
How he cared for God's people.

709
00:48:42,980 --> 00:48:44,320
No matter where he found them.

710
00:48:44,320 --> 00:48:48,520
Eat this if you're a follower of Jesus.

711
00:48:48,520 --> 00:48:49,720
And remember his life.

712
00:48:49,720 --> 00:49:07,000
And this is the high risk part.

713
00:49:07,000 --> 00:49:11,220
We're going to gingerly open this.

714
00:49:14,460 --> 00:49:15,460
Around the iPad.

715
00:49:15,460 --> 00:49:18,500
Pro tip for next week.

716
00:49:18,500 --> 00:49:20,260
Once the cracker's out of the way.

717
00:49:20,260 --> 00:49:22,300
Just stab two holes in it with a pencil.

718
00:49:28,380 --> 00:49:32,080
We're going to take the juice and think about Jesus' blood.

719
00:49:32,080 --> 00:49:34,600
Which is kind of dumb.

720
00:49:34,600 --> 00:49:43,620
But we're going to think about how because we turn to Jesus and because he calls us out to seek him.

721
00:49:43,620 --> 00:49:45,680
Those who look to him.

722
00:49:45,680 --> 00:49:47,200
God has forgiven them.

723
00:49:47,960 --> 00:49:49,600
And we have peace and unity with God.

724
00:49:49,600 --> 00:49:51,060
And we're members of his kingdom.

725
00:49:51,060 --> 00:49:54,760
And it's because that gift was given.

726
00:49:54,760 --> 00:49:56,680
It's because that gift was born.

727
00:49:56,680 --> 00:49:58,360
Born into poverty.

728
00:49:58,360 --> 00:49:59,520
Born lonely.

729
00:49:59,520 --> 00:50:01,560
In a weird time in history.

730
00:50:01,560 --> 00:50:04,720
That we can celebrate the man who grew out of that.

731
00:50:04,720 --> 00:50:08,720
And we look at his blood and see that God made something huge out of this.

732
00:50:08,720 --> 00:50:09,660
And it was part of his plan.

733
00:50:11,520 --> 00:50:12,480
So take the cup.

734
00:50:12,480 --> 00:50:14,880
Knowing that your sins are forgiven.

735
00:50:14,880 --> 00:50:16,420
Not because we're doing this.

736
00:50:16,420 --> 00:50:17,440
But because of what Christ did.

737
00:50:17,440 --> 00:50:36,160
Finally.

738
00:50:36,160 --> 00:50:37,560
And I use that word loosely.

739
00:50:40,020 --> 00:50:44,400
We can relate to those who waited for Jesus because we're waiting for another king.

740
00:50:44,400 --> 00:50:45,980
The same king in another form.

741
00:50:45,980 --> 00:50:48,140
We're waiting for him to come down.

742
00:50:48,140 --> 00:50:51,440
And this historically has been a major theme of Advent.

743
00:50:51,440 --> 00:50:53,940
Where we kind of remember forward.

744
00:50:53,940 --> 00:50:56,680
We look back at God's people of anticipation for Christ.

745
00:50:56,680 --> 00:50:59,120
And we recognize that this is the time of the year.

746
00:50:59,120 --> 00:51:00,300
The only time of the year.

747
00:51:00,300 --> 00:51:02,520
When the church historically has said.

748
00:51:02,520 --> 00:51:05,720
Let's think about when Jesus comes back.

749
00:51:05,720 --> 00:51:08,740
Let's think about when this kingdom that he planted.

750
00:51:08,740 --> 00:51:11,140
That has been growing and growing and growing ever since.

751
00:51:11,140 --> 00:51:15,900
That has seen victory and struggle and scandal and embarrassment.

752
00:51:15,900 --> 00:51:19,140
That kingdom is going to flower and fruit someday.

753
00:51:19,140 --> 00:51:21,200
And God's going to come back.

754
00:51:21,200 --> 00:51:22,500
And Christ will live with us.

755
00:51:22,500 --> 00:51:23,340
And be with us.

756
00:51:23,340 --> 00:51:27,260
That's a big deal.

757
00:51:27,260 --> 00:51:30,240
Let me read one passage.

758
00:51:31,540 --> 00:51:32,960
From the very end of the Bible.

759
00:51:32,960 --> 00:51:34,880
This is Revelation 21.

760
00:51:34,880 --> 00:51:40,340
Then I saw a new heaven and a new earth.

761
00:51:40,340 --> 00:51:43,960
For the first heaven and the first earth had passed away.

762
00:51:43,960 --> 00:51:45,100
And the sea was no more.

763
00:51:45,100 --> 00:51:47,680
And I saw the holy city, New Jerusalem.

764
00:51:47,680 --> 00:51:49,340
Coming down out of heaven from God.

765
00:51:49,340 --> 00:51:51,860
Prepared as a bride adorned for her husband.

766
00:51:52,520 --> 00:51:54,800
And I heard a loud voice on the throne.

767
00:51:54,800 --> 00:51:57,340
Saying, Behold, the dwelling place of God is with man.

768
00:51:57,340 --> 00:51:58,960
He is dwelling with them.

769
00:51:58,960 --> 00:52:00,680
He will be with his people.

770
00:52:00,680 --> 00:52:03,440
And God himself will be with them as their God.

771
00:52:03,440 --> 00:52:05,940
He will wipe away every tear from their eyes.

772
00:52:05,940 --> 00:52:07,560
And death shall be no more.

773
00:52:07,560 --> 00:52:08,860
Neither shall there be mourning.

774
00:52:08,860 --> 00:52:09,940
Nor crying.

775
00:52:09,940 --> 00:52:11,480
Nor pain anymore.

776
00:52:11,480 --> 00:52:13,880
For the former things have passed away.

777
00:52:14,360 --> 00:52:20,400
And he who is seated on the throne said, Behold, I am making all things new.

778
00:52:20,400 --> 00:52:26,360
That's the promise of Christmas.

779
00:52:26,360 --> 00:52:27,360
That's the promise of Advent.

780
00:52:27,360 --> 00:52:30,440
Is that we're not looking backwards in a baby.

781
00:52:30,440 --> 00:52:33,420
We're looking forward to another king.

782
00:52:33,420 --> 00:52:34,880
Who's going to come be with us.

783
00:52:34,880 --> 00:52:38,140
He's going to make untrue all the things that are wrong and painful.

784
00:52:38,140 --> 00:52:40,100
And he's going to make all things new.

785
00:52:40,100 --> 00:52:42,500
Let's pray.

786
00:52:43,020 --> 00:52:47,780
Heavenly Father, we sang earlier that our hearts will sing no other name.

787
00:52:47,780 --> 00:52:51,540
But we sang it aspirationally as something to aspire to.

788
00:52:51,540 --> 00:52:53,880
Because our hearts sing dozens of other names that are less than you.

789
00:52:53,880 --> 00:52:57,960
And so, help us to focus on the other part of the song.

790
00:52:57,960 --> 00:53:00,840
Where we call in the light of the world to forever reign.

791
00:53:00,840 --> 00:53:05,240
Lord, this Christmas, help us to focus on you as the light of the world.

792
00:53:05,240 --> 00:53:07,360
And that your kingdom is coming forever.

793
00:53:07,360 --> 00:53:09,780
And it started, the seed was a little baby.

794
00:53:09,780 --> 00:53:12,620
And it grew up into something magnificent and humble.

795
00:53:13,500 --> 00:53:18,380
Lord, help us to go into this week magnificently and humbly.

796
00:53:18,380 --> 00:53:20,880
And may your kingdom forever reign.

797
00:53:20,880 --> 00:53:22,020
Amen.
